  "result": {
    "session_id": "eval-20260427_190913-12-init-fail",
    "query_id": "12-init-fail",
    "messages": [
      {
        "role": "user",
        "content": "The deployment app-with-init in namespace scenario-test is stuck and never reaches Running state. The main application container never starts. Investigate why and identify the blocking component."
      }
    ],
    "final_text": "TARGETED: namespace=scenario-test, pod=app-with-init-7965877949-ms2f6, issue=Init container blocking main application startupThe issue is already clear from the snapshot: the init container `db-check` in the pod `app-with-init-7965877949-ms2f6` is failing repeatedly with a `CrashLoopBackOff` state. This is preventing the main application container from starting.\n\n### Root Cause\nThe init container `db-check` is attempting to check database connectivity using the command:\n```sh\nnc -zw3 db.internal.svc.cluster.local 5432 || exit 1\n```\nThis command fails because the host `db.internal.svc.cluster.local` does not exist or is unreachable. As a result, the init container exits with code `1`, causing the pod to remain in the `Init:0/1` state.\n\n### Blocking Component\nThe blocking component is the init container `db-check`. Its failure prevents the pod from progressing to the main application container startup.\n\n### Recommendation\nTo resolve this issue:\n1. Verify the intended database service (`db.internal.svc.cluster.local`) exists and is correctly configured.\n2. If the database service is not required, remove the init container from the deployment.\n3. If the database service is required but not yet deployed, deploy it and ensure it is reachable from the pod.\n\nWould you like me to:\n- Check if the database service exists in the cluster?\n- Patch the deployment to remove the init container?",
